Chapter: GopHandoffTest
  cites Works chapter GopAcpi
  cites Works chapter GopHandoff

 Three arms over the magic gate on the 0x1F000 handoff block. The block is
 written here rather than by a stub, so the arms differ only in the magic
 quadword and the middle arm is the one that must move. Nothing outside
 0x1F000..0x1F02F is written: acpi-cell is 0x8000, where the PML4 lives, and
 a write there would take the page tables with it.

Section: Fixture

 The magic bytes are ASCII "CDXHANDF" and the sentinel is 0x000E0000, the
 value the real bed reports for the RSDP, little-endian in both cases.

  gh-write-magic : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  gh-write-magic (dummy) = act
    poke-byte handoff-base 0 67
    poke-byte handoff-base 1 68
    poke-byte handoff-base 2 88
    poke-byte handoff-base 3 72
    poke-byte handoff-base 4 65
    poke-byte handoff-base 5 78
    poke-byte handoff-base 6 68
    poke-byte handoff-base 7 70
  end

  gh-clear-magic : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  gh-clear-magic (dummy) = act
    poke-byte handoff-base 0 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 1 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 2 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 3 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 4 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 5 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 6 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 7 0
  end

  gh-write-rsdp : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  gh-write-rsdp (dummy) = act
    poke-byte handoff-base 40 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 41 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 42 14
    poke-byte handoff-base 43 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 44 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 45 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 46 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 47 0
  end

 Width 1920 and height 1080 share the quadword at +0x18, stride 2048 and
 format 1 the one at +0x20. Those are the real board's numbers, and the
 padded stride is the case that shears if the halves are read the wrong way
 round.

  gh-write-mode : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  gh-write-mode (dummy) = act
    poke-byte handoff-base 24 128
    poke-byte handoff-base 25 7
    poke-byte handoff-base 26 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 27 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 28 56
    poke-byte handoff-base 29 4
    poke-byte handoff-base 30 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 31 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 32 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 33 8
    poke-byte handoff-base 34 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 35 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 36 1
    poke-byte handoff-base 37 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 38 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 39 0
  end

  gh-write-fb : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  gh-write-fb (dummy) = act
    poke-byte handoff-base 16 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 17 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 18 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 19 191
    poke-byte handoff-base 20 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 21 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 22 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 23 0
  end

  gh-clear-fb : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  gh-clear-fb (dummy) = act
    poke-byte handoff-base 16 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 17 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 18 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 19 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 20 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 21 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 22 0
    poke-byte handoff-base 23 0
  end

Section: Main

  opening : [Console, Device.Mmio] Nothing
  opening =
    let old = peek-qword acpi-cell 40
    in act
      gh-clear-magic 0
      print-line-uni ("absent: " & show (handoff-present 0) & " " & show (acpi-boot-rsdp 0 == old))
      gh-write-magic 0
      gh-write-rsdp 0
      print-line-uni ("present: " & show (handoff-present 0) & " " & show (acpi-boot-rsdp 0))
      gh-write-mode 0
      gh-write-fb 0
      print-line-uni ("mode: " & show (handoff-w 0) & " " & show (handoff-h 0) & " " & show (handoff-stride 0))
      print-line-uni ("fb: " & show (handoff-fb-base 0))
      gh-clear-fb 0
      print-line-uni ("nofb: " & show (handoff-present 0) & " " & show (handoff-fb-base 0))
      poke-byte handoff-base 7 71
      print-line-uni ("corrupt: " & show (handoff-present 0) & " " & show (acpi-boot-rsdp 0 == old))
      gh-clear-magic 0
      print-line-uni "done"
    end
